2. STRICT PROHIBITION ON COMMERCIAL AND OEM USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE SOFTWARE, ITS ARCHITECTURAL CONCEPTS, INTERFACES, AND ALGORITHMS ARE STRICTLY PROTECTED UNDER INTERNATIONAL COPYRIGHT AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY LAWS.

(a) NO COMMERCIAL USE: You may not sell, rent, lease, sublicense, distribute for a fee, monetize, or exploit the Software or any portion thereof directly or indirectly in any commercial product, service, or distribution platform.
(b) NO OEM OR HARDWARE VENDOR INTEGRATION: Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs), smartphone manufacturers, camera module vendors, chipset vendors, commercial ROM developers, and commercial mobile application developers are STRICTLY PROHIBITED from:
    (i) Pre-installing, bundling, or integrating this Software into any firmware, system ROM, operating system, or device image;
    (ii) Copying, reimplementing, reverse-engineering, cloning, or patenting the user interface concepts, layouts, architectures, and algorithms developed herein, including but not limited to:
        - The Dual-Corner Viewfinder HUD architecture, comprising:
          * Direct manual sensor and optical controls located in the bottom-left corner of the live viewfinder (In-Sensor Zoom 1.0x-2.0x, multi-step and continuous physical variable aperture f/1.63-f/4.0 switcher, and focus drive selector);
          * The Top-Right Viewfinder Advanced Control & Telemetry Suite ("Правая верхняя шторка / Оверлей"), incorporating:
            - Real-time hardware execution and platform badge indicator (HEX for Qualcomm Hexagon DSP FastRPC vector offload, CPU fallback, and purple Mediatek indicator when Sabre MTK is active);
            - HDR+ Enhanced frame accumulation queue and processing readiness indicator;
            - Live spatial and temporal luma/chroma denoise mode selector and adaptive ISO tier control;
            - Hot-swappable tone-mapping selector (native _StartTone / _StartGamma curve injection with controlled session reload, plus instant NEON-accelerated Cupertino SmartTone mode);
            - Hot-swappable color space & live Chroma Vibrance engine (on-the-fly switching between sRGB and DCI-P3 Wide Gamut / Display P3 EXIF 0xFFFF ICC embedding paired with instant ARM64 NEON Chroma-Gated Vibrance);
            - Multi-engine White Balance (AWB) switcher (Google Neural AWB, Sony IMX686 / Hardware Sensor profiles, Config XML, and Native Camera2 ISP with genuine SENSOR_NEUTRAL_COLOR_POINT reliance);
            - Real-time Color Calibration Suite (Saturation presets, Hardware Black Level 64/32/0 selection, Perceptual System Color Vibrance preserving rowSum = 1.0 neutral greys without AUX double-saturation);
            - Parametric exposure bracketing engine (Auto with Gyroscope + OIS Handheld vs. Tripod shutter guard, curated HDR presets, and manual multi-series configuration with customizable frame count and Delta EV step);
            - In-viewfinder profile and configuration management system (on-the-fly switching between embedded APK profiles, Hardware-First AutoCalibrator profiles, and custom XML presets without exiting camera preview);
            - Per-lens AutoCalibrator diagnostic and control panel (Applied vs. Kept summary, two-decimal sensor pixel pitch readout, and independent per-camera AutoCalibrator toggles);
        - The Hardware-First Per-Lens AutoCalibrator architecture (5-step hardware profiling across all physical lenses, <4 MP stub camera filtering, Smartphone-Only 429 Noise / 45 Color compact model catalogs, optics-aware sharpness preservation > 1 and unconditional Shasta preservation, per-camera Session OpMode matching with onConfigureFailed quarantine recovery, non-Xiaomi fix_resolution_key=37 protection, and zero-rescan cold-start hardware caching);
        - The ARM64 NEON JPEG Post-Processing Engine (libmakcam_turbojpeg.so inline pipeline implementing selective Soft-Highlight Knee at luma > 212 without shadow darkening, non-linear Chroma-Gated Vibrance preserving neutral greys and skin tones, Cupertino SmartTone curve transfer, APP2 ICC preservation, and lossless Huffman optimization);
        - The MediaTek Sabre MTK Runtime Auto-Patch Engine (automatic Dimensity/Helio SoC detection, stock-byte verification, dynamic libgcastartup.so native patching, and dedicated Mediatek HUD status indicator);
        - The multi-generational Hexagon FastRPC DSP probe & QNN HTP / ONNX Runtime / TFLite integration;
        - The HudI18n dynamic overlay localization engine synchronizing Dual-Corner HUD and modal dialogs with active system APK locales;
        - The integrated multi-step and continuous physical aperture switcher.
(c) Any such commercial integration, licensing, or adoption requires a separate, formal, prior written licensing agreement executed directly with Vseslav Makarov.

